IMPORT prelude

-- Row il-65. NOUNS of the two things this row records (items I1 and I2) in the Sale (Apartments) (Assurance of Investments of Persons Acquiring Apartments) Law, 5735-1974 (called "the Assurance Law" in this row): a defined term that a definition cites by a name, and an instruction that replaces a string of words.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: what the sources do not answer is not asked.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Assurance Law. It records two things, as typed values the tests check, and keeps each defect as an expected-red test.
-- The names of the fields below are mine, not the Law's. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module: `src:` lines are the consolidations (excerpts, deposited), `ext:[...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument.
-- A reading whose two sides differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.

§ `Nouns of a reading`

-- Where a reading comes from, from the stronger to the weaker.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official page, read from its image, and the cropped image is deposited`
    `the consolidation only`

§ `Nouns of a citation (I1)`

-- A citation by name: the words that cite, the name they print, the name the target prints, and how many of the things named the target has under that name.
DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `what the citing words name` IS A STRING
    `the name as the citing words print it` IS A STRING
    `the name as the target prints it` IS A STRING
    `how many things the citing words name` IS A NUMBER
    `how many of them the target has under that name` IS A NUMBER
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of an instruction that replaces words (I2)`

-- How a place in a paragraph spells the words that an instruction names. The prefix is one letter, written on the first word and on the last.
DECLARE `How a place spells the words` IS ONE OF
    `exactly as the instruction names them`
    `as the instruction names them, with a one-letter prefix on the first word and on the last`

DECLARE `An instruction that replaces words` HAS
    `the instrument and its section` IS A STRING
    `the subsection the instruction names` IS A STRING
    `how the instruction says it applies` IS A STRING
    `the string the instruction replaces` IS A STRING
    `the words the instruction puts in its place` IS A STRING
    `the instruction was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

-- A place in the subsection where the words of the instruction may stand. The two revisions are the consolidation's own, named by their ids; the row says nothing about when the instruction takes effect.
DECLARE `A place that holds words` HAS
    `where the place is` IS A STRING
    `the lines read` IS A STRING
    `the words at the place in revision 2968704` IS A STRING
    `the words at the place in revision 3085793` IS A STRING
    `how the place spells the words in revision 2968704` IS A `How a place spells the words`
    `the places were read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
